{"schemaVersion":2,"sectionID":20019733,"chapterID":15000907,"chapterNumber":"IX-7","sectionNumber":"97-411","title":"Maximum floor area ratio within the Core Subdistrict","officialText":"","previewText":"In C4-4D, C4-7 or C6-3 Districts in the Core Subdistrict, as shown on Map 1 in Appendix A of this Chapter, the maximum permitted floor area ratios shall be as listed in the following table for residential, commercial and community facility uses.\n\nSeparate residential floor area ratios are set forth for zoning lots containing standard residences and zoning lots containing qualifying affordable housing or qualifying se","blocks":[{"id":"zr-19733-block-001","kind":"html","html":"<p>In C4-4D, C4-7 or C6-3 Districts in the Core Subdistrict, as shown on Map 1 in Appendix A of this Chapter, the maximum permitted <strong><em>floor area ratios</em></strong> shall be as listed in the following table for <strong><em>residential</em></strong>, <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> and <strong><em>community facility</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong>.</p>","plainText":"In C4-4D, C4-7 or C6-3 Districts in the Core Subdistrict, as shown on Map 1 in Appendix A of this Chapter, the maximum permitted floor area ratios shall be as listed in the following table for residential, commercial and community facility uses."},{"id":"zr-19733-block-002","kind":"html","html":"<p>Separate <strong><em>residential</em></strong> <strong><em>floor area ratios</em></strong> are set forth for <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> containing standard <strong><em>residences</em></strong> and <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> containing <strong><em>qualifying affordable housing</em></strong> or <strong><em>qualifying senior housing</em></strong>.</p>","plainText":"Separate residential floor area ratios are set forth for zoning lots containing standard residences and zoning lots containing qualifying affordable housing or qualifying senior housing."},{"id":"zr-19733-block-003","kind":"html","html":"<p>The <strong><em>residential</em></strong> <strong><em>floor area ratios</em></strong> or <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>floor area ratios</em></strong> may be increased up to the applicable maximum <strong><em>floor area ratios</em></strong> in the following table, provided that for every four square feet of bonused <strong><em>floor area</em></strong>, an amount of space equivalent to one square foot of such bonused <strong><em>floor area</em></strong> shall be used for those visual or performing arts <strong><em>uses</em></strong> designated in paragraph (b) of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ix/chapter-7#97-11\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ix/chapter-7#97-11\"><span>97-11</span></a> (Special Arts and Entertainment Uses). Such bonused <strong><em>floor area</em></strong> shall be permitted only upon certification by the Chairperson of the City Planning Commission to the Commissioner of Buildings that the conditions set forth in Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ix/chapter-7#97-42\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ix/chapter-7#97-42\"><span>97-42</span></a> have been met.</p>","plainText":"The residential floor area ratios or commercial floor area ratios may be increased up to the applicable maximum floor area ratios in the following table, provided that for every four square feet of bonused floor area, an amount of space equivalent to one square foot of such bonused floor area shall be used for those visual or performing arts uses designated in paragraph (b) of Section 97-11 (Special Arts and Entertainment Uses). Such bonused floor area shall be permitted only upon certification by the Chairperson of the City Planning Commission to the Commissioner of Buildings that the conditions set forth in Section 97-42 have been met."},{"id":"zr-19733-block-004","kind":"html","html":"<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">MAXIMUM PERMITTED FLOOR AREA RATIO (FAR) FOR RESIDENTIAL,<br>\nCOMMERCIAL AND COMMUNITY FACILITY USES</span></span></p>","plainText":"MAXIMUM PERMITTED FLOOR AREA RATIO (FAR) FOR RESIDENTIAL, COMMERCIAL AND COMMUNITY FACILITY USES"},{"id":"zr-19733-block-005","kind":"table","html":"<table class=\"Table\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border:none\" width=\"648\"><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"7\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:648px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:34px; border-top:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b>Within the Core Subdistrict</b></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:78px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:154px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">District</span></b></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:106px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:154px; border-top:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-left:none\" valign=\"top\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><strong><em>Residential Floor Area Ratio</em></strong> for Standard <strong><em>Residences</em></strong></span></b></span></span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; width:94px; padding:0in 7px 0in 7px; height:154px; border-top:none; border-right:1p